          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes a fabric suitable for restaurants and bars?",
            "answer": "<p>Restaurant and bar upholstery fabrics need to shrug off food, grease and drink spills, wipe clean quickly between covers, resist heavy daily wear and meet fire-safety requirements. Monteiro's restaurant fabrics are coated fabrics with a non-absorbent, wipe-clean surface that is grease- and stain-resistant, abrasion-resistant, flame-retardant and REACH-compliant.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are restaurant fabrics resistant to grease and food stains?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The coated surface is non-absorbent, so grease, food and drink spills sit on top rather than soaking in. Most marks lift away with a simple wipe, helping seating stay clean and presentable through a busy service.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How are these fabrics cleaned?",
            "answer": "<p>Simply wipe the surface down with a damp cloth and mild detergent to remove food, grease and drink spills. Avoid solvents and abrasive pads or cleaners, which can damage the coating.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do they meet fire-safety standards for hospitality venues?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The fabrics are flame-retardant and meet contract upholstery fire-safety standards, and they are REACH-compliant and phthalate-free. Ask our team for the specific certificates and test reports your venue requires.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where are these fabrics used?",
            "answer": "<p>They are specified for banquettes, booths, dining chairs, bar stools and café seating — anywhere in restaurants, bars and hospitality venues that demands hard-wearing, easy-to-wipe surfaces.</p>"
          }
        },
